Title:
Ghost — Process Injection & Memory Manipulation Detection (Rust)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
Ghost is a cross-platform (Windows-focused) userspace tool for detecting process injection and in-memory tampering by scanning live processes for suspicious memory and execution artifacts. It targets common tradecraft such as RWX/unbacked executable regions, shellcode-like instruction patterns, process hollowing, API hooking (inline/IAT), thread hijacking, and APC injection, with optional YARA-based signature matching. The project provides both a CLI and an interactive TUI, plus continuous “watch” mode, baseline comparison, JSON output, and webhook alerting (Slack/Discord/generic HTTP). Detections are scored with confidence and mapped to MITRE ATT&CK techniques to support reporting and triage workflows. It’s primarily useful for Blue Teams, threat hunters, incident responders, and malware analysts; Red Teams can use it to validate whether their injection techniques are detectable. Interesting aspects include multi-OS support, configurable detection pipelines, and an emphasis on reducing false positives via corroboration requirements for “Malicious” verdicts.

Technical Focus:
- Process enumeration and memory region inspection (Windows/Linux/macOS)
- Detection of injected code artifacts (RWX, unbacked exec, shellcode heuristics)
- Process hollowing and PE validation (Windows)
- Hook detection (inline patching, IAT modifications; LD_PRELOAD/DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES)
- Thread analysis for hijacking/APC-style execution redirection
- YARA rule integration and ATT&CK technique mapping

Use Cases:
- Hunt for in-memory implants and injection activity on endpoints
- Continuous monitoring with alerting to Slack/Discord/SIEM via webhooks
- Baseline-vs-current comparisons to surface new or escalated suspicious processes
- Validate EDR bypass/injection PoCs against heuristic detections (red team testing)
- Triage suspicious processes with structured indicators and JSON output for automation

Keywords:
Rust, process injection detection, memory scanning, RWX memory, unbacked executable memory, shellcode heuristics, process hollowing, API hooking, inline hooks, IAT patching, thread hijacking, APC injection, YARA, MITRE ATT&CK, Windows PE validation, procfs, ptrace, mach VM APIs, LD_PRELOAD, DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES, webhook alerts, TUI, baseline mode, threat hunting